1. The grant, VERBATIM from the font binary
-------------------------------------------

Extracted from unifont.ttf's own OpenType `name` table, record 0 (Copyright), rather than
transcribed from a website — this is what the binary we redistribute actually carries:

    Copyright (C) 2014 Roman Czyborra, Paul Hardy, Qianqian Fang, Andrew Miller, et al.
    Licensed under the GNU General Public License; either version 2, or (at your option) a
    later version, with the GNU Font Embedding Exception.

The GPL version 2 text is in this directory as GPL-2.


2. The GNU Font Embedding Exception, VERBATIM — read the provenance note
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

Unifont's binary NAMES this exception but does not carry its text. The paragraph below is the
standard exception, reproduced verbatim from a different font in this same content tree:
data/font-xolonium.pk3dir/fonts/xolonium-regular.otf, `name` table record 13, which is also
GPLv2+ with this same exception and does ship the full wording. It appears there identically in
both the Macintosh (record 13, platform 1) and Windows (record 13, platform 3, UTF-16BE)
encodings, which is a useful cross-check that it was not garbled in extraction.

    As a special exception, if you create a document which uses this font, and embed this font
    or unaltered portions of this font into the document, this font does not by itself cause
    the resulting document to be covered by the GNU General Public License. This exception does
    not however invalidate any other reasons why the document might be covered by the GNU
    General Public License. If you modify this font, you may extend this exception to your
    version of the font, but you are not obligated to do so. If you do not wish to do so,
    delete this exception statement from your version.

**Where this copy came from is stated plainly above and deliberately.** It is a real, verbatim
copy of the standard exception, not a paraphrase and not written from memory — but it was taken
from Xolonium's binary, not Unifont's, because Unifont's does not contain it. Anyone who wants
the text from Unifont's own distribution should take it from unifoundry.com's release of 7.0.06
and replace this section. That is a strictly better source; it is simply not one that exists
anywhere in this repository.


3. A trap: do NOT take this font's terms from unifoundry.com today
-------------------------------------------------------------------

Checked 2026-07-30: unifoundry.com's current LICENSE.txt states that compiled fonts are under
the **SIL Open Font License v1.1** plus the font embedding exception. That describes a LATER
release than the one we ship. The binary in this tree is version 7.0.06 (2014) and declares
GPLv2-or-later in its own name table, as quoted in section 1.

A binary is governed by the terms it was released under, not by the terms its upstream project
adopted afterwards. Reading today's licence page and applying it to a 2014 font would attach the
wrong licence to this file. If Unifont is ever upgraded here, re-derive this notice from the new
binary rather than assuming either licence carried over.


Provenance of this file
